  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What a view records",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "content": "Values are shown masked first; a person who may see them whole reveals them with a reason. Every reveal is audited as `records_viewed` with:\n\n- its **purpose**, from a fixed list, and its **reference** (a ticket or case number) when one was given;\n- its **job**, how many **rows** it showed and the **names of the fields** it showed: never a value.\n\nViews audited before reveals asked for a reason have none of these and read as *not recorded*. A masked read is not a view and is not listed. There is no way to export personal data. A view is known by its resource and its shape, **not by which clients** it showed.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Views over time, by kind",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
